# Development-only credentials. Copy to `.env.local`, never commit a real key.
#
# Used by exactly one thing: `connectFluid()`'s fallback, which calls the
# provider directly when no wallet answers and NODE_ENV is not "production".
# It exists so a page can be worked on without loading the extension. It is a
# convenience, never a security boundary — the whole point of the wallet is that
# pages do not hold keys, so do not point this at a key you care about.
FLUID_DEV_API_KEY=

# The browser bundle has no `process.env`, so an app that wants the fallback has
# to hand the value across. For Vite:
#
#   VITE_FLUID_DEV_API_KEY=
#   connectFluid({ devApiKey: import.meta.env.VITE_FLUID_DEV_API_KEY })
#
# For Next.js the name above works as-is in server code; in a client component
# it needs the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix. Either way the key ends up in the bundle —
# which is precisely the arrangement the wallet exists to remove.
